WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
- I love your outfit!

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.870
I asked her, she did a "get ready" video,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.220
like coming out here.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.053
- Always.

00:00:06.053 --> 00:00:06.990
- Okay, I cannot wait to see this.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.760
You have six million followers.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.593
- Yes.

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:10.426
- That's incredible.

00:00:10.426 --> 00:00:12.120
Okay, so explain "get ready with me."

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.953
Did that just-

00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:13.890
you were just doing it for fun and then

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.630
it ended up becoming
like a segment almost?

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.640
- Yeah, so on TikTok, you can do like

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.320
a livestream video and I would always

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.309
do those before I was going out and

00:00:21.309 --> 00:00:24.270
those videos would get way more views

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.550
and way more traction than my-

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.390
oh, oh my gosh.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.223
- [Kelly] There you are.

00:00:28.223 --> 00:00:29.056
(Alix giggles)

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:30.210
- They would get more views than

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.890
the videos I was posting on TikTok,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.723
so I was like, "you know what,

00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:34.950
why don't I just turn
these getting ready videos

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.050
into a TikTok video?"

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.050
And they just took off.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.010
It's crazy to me.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.140
I guess people are just interested,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.670
and I do my makeup while I'm kind of

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.230
talking about where I'm going

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.110
or what's going on and
a lot of it would be

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.120
me at the University of Miami,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.430
night life in Miami, what is Miami like,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.651
and I think it's just a crazy universe

00:00:55.651 --> 00:00:57.810
down in Miami so people were just

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.350
so interested and took off from there.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.424
- I like, though, when you-

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:04.170
I think breaking down the wall, that's the

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.730
reason why people get into it, as well,

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.197
because people like to see people

00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:08.523
that are relatable, I think.

00:01:08.523 --> 00:01:10.200
- Yeah.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.240
- Well, one of Alix's "get ready with me"

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.170
posts that went viral -

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.070
oh, this is amazing -

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.890
was her getting ready for
a Miami Dolphins game.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.723
So let's see that.

00:01:17.723 --> 00:01:18.556
I love it.

00:01:18.556 --> 00:01:21.090
- I have this tiny little Jimmy Choo bag,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.560
which I think goes with the heels.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.865
Feel like a mom picking
up her kids from school.

00:01:25.865 --> 00:01:28.698
(audience cheers)

00:01:30.526 --> 00:01:31.443
- I'm like.

00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:36.601
I love that you think a mom
could look that together

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:37.500
picking up-

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.550
I know, it's amazing.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.190
So the moms, they came out.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.290
- The moms humbled me very quickly.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.210
They were like, "girl."

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.160
- [Kelly] Yep, yep.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.390
Yeah.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.339
This is on the way to school.

00:01:52.339 --> 00:01:54.142
This is them on-

00:01:54.142 --> 00:01:56.725
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.403
Okay.

00:01:58.403 --> 00:01:59.700
So this is me after-

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.936
yes, yeah.

00:02:00.936 --> 00:02:02.926
This is, you see the-

00:02:02.926 --> 00:02:05.759
(audience cheers)

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.460
This is me.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.560
This is after sleeping with your children

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.020
and they kick you all night

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.040
and it's super fun.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.080
No, my goal is to look like you

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.060
in that video at some point.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.530
So wait, so you have a new podcast.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.640
This is like a new realm for you,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.481
so do you like it?

00:02:21.481 --> 00:02:22.314
Are you enjoying it?

00:02:22.314 --> 00:02:23.147
- I love it.

00:02:23.147 --> 00:02:26.520
It's been a learning process for sure.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.050
You know, 'cause when you're
talking for two minutes

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.000
in a TikTok video and now I'm talking for

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.760
two hours for one episode to come out,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.520
it's very different and I think people are

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.320
getting to see a different side of me

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.080
or just learning so much about me

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.390
that they didn't know before and, I mean,

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.120
there's many more stories to come.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.599
- Does it stress you out
to be that vulnerable?

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.560
'Cause it's a little more
in-depth, I feel like,

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.393
the podcast.

00:02:50.393 --> 00:02:52.440
- Yeah, so right before I
launched the first episode,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.273
I was freaking out.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.510
I was like, "I don't think I can do this,

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.910
I'm so stressed," because
the more you tell people,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.580
the more room there is
for criticism and stuff,

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.100
but the reason I feel comfortable with

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.070
sharing my life online is just that

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.770
I feel like I'm kinda
directing the narrative of it

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.350
and I'm okay with people not liking me

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.101
if they don't like who I am, yeah.

00:03:13.101 --> 00:03:15.540
It's a little bit more frustrating when

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.800
there's false stuff out there,

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.633
and then I'm like-

00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:19.020
- It's so frustrating!

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.300
- But it's important to me to kind of

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.690
help the younger audience
that's watching me, too.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.058
I wish I had someone who was kinda of

00:03:27.058 --> 00:03:29.381
showing their acne or telling about

00:03:29.381 --> 00:03:31.500
getting cheated on, you
know, all that stuff

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.470
to look up to when I was younger, so I-

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.150
- [Kelly] And to connect to, yeah.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.500
- Hopefully setting a good example.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.700
- Yeah, well, good luck with it.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.990
Six episodes in, that's really awesome.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.823
- [Alix] Thank you.

00:03:40.823 --> 00:03:41.656
- Yeah, it is a lot of work, I heard.

00:03:41.656 --> 00:03:42.910
That's why I don't wanna do one.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.100
(audience and Alix laugh)

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.020
We did the math, though, and during the

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.110
course of just this segment, Alix has

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.830
gained over 5,000 followers, so just now.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.726
It just happened.

00:03:53.726 --> 00:03:54.750
(audience cheers)

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.583
It's amazing.

00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:57.720
Let's do a commercial break, everybody!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.090
You can listen to "Hot
Mess" with Alix Earle

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.533
every Thursday on Spotify.

